rs. Figure 2 photograph shows an example meter label reading DN25, Q3=2.5 m³/h, R=1600, U=3.6 V, MAP 16, T50.\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": \"Smartio\",\n    \"models\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN20_Q3=2.5_R630\", \"label\": \"Smartio DN20, Q3 = 2.5 m³/h, R 630\", \"attributes\": {\"nominal_diameter\": 20, \"q3\": 2.5, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 630}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN20_Q3=4.0_R630\", \"label\": \"Smartio DN20, Q3 = 4.0 m³/h, R 630\", \"attributes\": {\"nominal_diameter\": 20, \"q3\": 4.0, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 630}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN20_Q3=4.0_R800\", \"label\": \"Smartio DN20, Q3 = 4.0 m³/h, R 800\", \"attributes\": {\"nominal_diameter\": 20, \"q3\": 4.0, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 800}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN20_Q3=4.0_R1000\", \"label\": \"Smartio DN20, Q3 = 4.0 m³/h, R 1000\", \"attributes\": {\"nominal_diameter\": 20, \"q3\": 4.0, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 1000}}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Type details of the Smartio water meter variants\",\n      \"columns\": [\"model\", \"q1\", \"q2\", \"q3\", \"q4\", \"q3_q1_ratio\"],\n      \"column_units\": [null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null],\n      \"rows\": [\n        {\"model\": \"DN20_Q3=2.5_R630\", \"q1\": 0.004, \"q2\": 0.006, \"q3\": 2.5, \"q4\": 3.125, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 630},\n        {\"model\": \"DN20_Q3=4.0_R630\", \"q1\": 0.006, \"q2\": 0.01, \"q3\": 4.0, \"q4\": 5.0, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 630},\n        {\"model\": \"DN20_Q3=4.0_R800\", \"q1\": 0.005, \"q2\": 0.008, \"q3\": 4.0, \"q4\": 5.0, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 800},\n        {\"model\": \"DN20_Q3=4.0_R1000\", \"q1\": 0.004, \"q2\": 0.006, \"q3\": 4.0, \"q4\": 5.0, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 1000}\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Manufacturer: JANZ - Contagem e Gestao de Fluídos, S.A.; model name: Smartio; nominal diameter: 20 (mm), common to all variants. In the source table the Q3/Q1 ratio 630 spans the first two variants (colspan 2); the following columns are 800 and 1000.\",\n      \"footnotes\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R49\",\n    \"edition\": 2013,\n    \"scheme\": \"A\"\n  },\n  \"revision_history\": [\n    {\"revision\": \"20-001\"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nWait — characteristics section: schema has characteristics with type_level, model_level, config_level. Should I include nominal_diameter as type_level? Yes:\n\n```json\n\"characteristics\": {\n  \"type_level\": {\n    \"nominal_diameter\": {\"value\": 20, \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\", \"unit_id\": null}\n  },\n  \"model_level\": [...]\n}\n```\n\nAnd model_level entries for q1..q4 and ratio.\n\nShould footnote_markers be included in value entries? Optional; omit where none.\n\nShould \"footnotes\": [] be included in matrix_tables? The schema shows footnotes[] — empty is fine or omit. I'll omit empty arrays to be clean. Actually including empty is fine but I'll omit.\n\nOne thing: category \"Water meter\" — matches the suggested list style (\"Gas meter\" is in the examples; water meter analog). Good.\n\nAlso, should I include \"scheme\": \"A\" in recommendation? The yaml: recommendation: id, edition, amendment, scheme, accuracy_classes[]. Scheme A from cert number. Include.\n\nCertificate \"scheme\": \"A\" — yes.\n\nAm I sure about the member_state? I'll keep it.\n\nAlso certificate.date_issued: \"24.06\" in the number might mean issued June 2024 but ambiguous; omit.\n\nDouble check decimal conversions: 0.010 → 0.01. Fine.\n\nJSON must be parseable — no markdown fences, just the object.",
